{
  "sampleRate": 22050,
  "notes": "Domino droid voice, whistle family: every emote is built like 'whistle' (the owner's reference, 2026-11-14) - smooth sine glides joined without gaps, a light octave-down body (sub 0.2), slow gentle vibrato on the held or falling part, mostly 1.2-3 kHz. Older sets are in sounds/archive. Each emote is a list of segments. wave: sine | tri | sq | fm | hop. f0->f1 is a glide in Hz over ms, then gap ms of silence. curve: lin | exp. vib/vibDepth: vibrato rate (Hz) and depth (fraction of pitch). sub: 0..1 mix of a second voice; subRatio sets its pitch relative to the main voice (default 0.5 = one octave down; about 1.06 beats into a screech). amp is 0..1. atk/rel: fade-in and fade-out in ms (default 4 and 8; longer is softer, flute-like). phrases string emotes together: a name plays that emote, a number is a pause in ms, {emote, pitch, tempo} plays it shifted. babble makes a long seeded whistle sentence at build time. Edit, then run: node sounds/build.mjs",
